<body>
<div class="noprint">Printable guide — use your browser's Print (two letter pages, black &amp; white).</div>

<svg width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute" aria-hidden="true">
  <defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#1d1f1c"/></marker></defs>
</svg>

<!-- ============ PAGE 1 ============ -->
<section class="page">
  <header><h1>Spinning Yarn on a Drop Spindle</h1><span class="brand">Waterbear Field School</span></header>
  <p class="lede">Spinning is just <b>twist</b> added to <b>loose fibre</b>. The spindle stores the twist; your hands decide how thick the yarn is. We'll use <b>park &amp; draft</b>: spin first, then stop the spindle and draft with both hands. It's the easiest way to learn. Sit in a firm chair without arms.</p>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">1</span> Know your spindle</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 130" role="img" aria-label="A top-whorl and a bottom-whorl spindle with labelled hook, whorl and shaft">
        <!-- top whorl -->
        <path class="l" d="M70 18 q0 -8 7 -8 q6 0 6 6"/>
        <line class="l" x1="70" y1="18" x2="70" y2="108"/>
        <ellipse class="f" cx="70" cy="30" rx="34" ry="7"/>
        <text class="lab" x="90" y="14">hook</text>
        <text class="lab" x="108" y="34">whorl</text>
        <text class="lab" x="78" y="90">shaft</text>
        <text class="lab" x="28" y="128" style="font-weight:400">top-whorl</text>
        <!-- bottom whorl -->
        <line class="l" x1="220" y1="10" x2="220" y2="108"/>
        <path class="l" d="M216 14 l4 -4 l4 4"/>
        <ellipse class="f" cx="220" cy="100" rx="34" ry="7"/>
        <text class="lab" x="228" y="16">notch</text>
        <text class="lab" x="258" y="104">whorl</text>
        <text class="lab" x="174" y="128" style="font-weight:400">bottom-whorl</text>
      </svg>
      <p>The <b>whorl</b> is the weight that keeps it spinning. Either kind works the same way. Always spin it <b>clockwise</b> (seen from above).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">2</span> Pre-draft the fibre</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 130" role="img" aria-label="Two hands gently pulling a strip of fibre apart so it thins and loosens">
        <path class="wool" d="M20 60 C60 40, 100 44, 150 56 C200 68, 240 72, 282 60 L282 82 C240 92, 200 86, 150 78 C100 70, 60 70, 20 84 Z"/>
        <path class="f" d="M70 46 q-14 4 -16 22 q2 18 18 22 q14 -2 16 -20 q-2 -20 -18 -24 z"/>
        <path class="f" d="M222 50 q-16 2 -18 22 q2 18 18 22 q14 -2 16 -20 q-2 -22 -16 -24 z"/>
        <path class="arrow" d="M44 112 L14 112"/>
        <path class="arrow" d="M254 112 L286 112"/>
        <text class="lab" x="118" y="30">thin, airy strip</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Split the fibre into finger-thick strips. Hold your hands a hand-width apart and pull <b>gently</b> along each strip until it's light and loose, but still in one piece.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">3</span> Tie on a leader</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 130" role="img" aria-label="A piece of yarn tied to the shaft below the whorl, brought up over the whorl and hooked">
        <line class="l" x1="110" y1="22" x2="110" y2="124"/>
        <path class="l" d="M110 22 q0 -8 7 -8 q6 0 6 6"/>
        <ellipse class="f" cx="110" cy="34" rx="34" ry="7"/>
        <path class="t" d="M110 50 q10 -3 0 6 q-10 3 0 -6" />
        <path class="t" d="M112 50 C150 46, 150 38, 142 34 C136 30, 128 26, 123 20 L118 14 C150 16, 170 30, 230 30" />
        <text class="lab" x="130" y="62">knot below whorl</text>
        <text class="lab" x="190" y="22">leader (~18 in)</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Tie a scrap of yarn (about 18 in) to the shaft <b>just below the whorl</b>. Bring it up over the edge of the whorl and once around the hook (or into the notch). This is the <b>leader</b>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">4</span> Join fibre to leader</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 130" role="img" aria-label="The fluffed end of the leader overlapping the fibre, held together while the spindle turns">
        <path class="t" d="M20 66 L120 66"/>
        <path class="t" d="M120 66 l20 -8 M120 66 l22 -2 M120 66 l22 4 M120 66 l20 10"/>
        <path class="wool" d="M128 52 C170 46, 230 44, 290 50 L290 84 C230 90, 170 86, 128 80 Z"/>
        <path class="f" d="M132 48 q-14 6 -14 20 q2 14 16 16 q14 -2 14 -18 q-2 -16 -16 -18 z"/>
        <text class="lab" x="20" y="56">leader</text>
        <text class="lab" x="236" y="42">fibre</text>
        <text class="lab" x="102" y="112">pinch the overlap</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Fluff out the end of the leader and lay it over the end of your fibre. Pinch the overlap, give the spindle a clockwise turn, and the twist will grab the two together.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step wide">
      <h2><span class="num">5</span> Spin it</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 620 120" role="img" aria-label="Rolling the spindle shaft up the thigh with the right hand to set it spinning clockwise">
        <path class="l" d="M60 96 C120 70, 220 64, 300 70"/>
        <path class="l" d="M60 112 C120 92, 220 88, 300 92"/>
        <text class="lab" x="306" y="96" style="font-weight:400">your thigh</text>
        <line class="l" x1="180" y1="18" x2="200" y2="82" />
        <ellipse class="f" cx="183" cy="28" rx="24" ry="6" transform="rotate(17 183 28)"/>
        <path class="arrow" d="M150 104 L250 72"/>
        <text class="lab" x="256" y="62">roll up the thigh</text>
        <!-- flick version -->
        <line class="l" x1="480" y1="10" x2="480" y2="96"/>
        <ellipse class="f" cx="480" cy="24" rx="30" ry="7"/>
        <path class="arrow" d="M446 60 A36 12 0 1 0 514 60"/>
        <text class="lab" x="524" y="50">clockwise</text>
        <text class="lab" x="436" y="114" style="font-weight:400">or flick the shaft</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Let the spindle hang. With your right hand, <b>roll the shaft up your right thigh</b> (or flick it with your fingers) so it turns clockwise. Hold the fibre in your left hand, with the leader running up to your fingers.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <footer><span>waterbearfieldschool.org</span><span>1 / 2</span></footer>
</section>

<!-- ============ PAGE 2 ============ -->
<section class="page">
  <header><h1>Park, Draft, Release, Repeat</h1><span class="brand">Waterbear Field School</span></header>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">6</span> Park it</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 140" role="img" aria-label="The spindle held still between the knees, with twisted yarn above">
        <path class="l" d="M40 60 C70 64, 110 80, 128 128"/>
        <path class="l" d="M260 60 C230 64, 190 80, 172 128"/>
        <text class="lab" x="20" y="54" style="font-weight:400">knee</text>
        <text class="lab" x="250" y="54" style="font-weight:400">knee</text>
        <line class="l" x1="150" y1="26" x2="150" y2="136"/>
        <ellipse class="f" cx="150" cy="38" rx="26" ry="6"/>
        <path class="t" d="M150 26 L150 4"/>
        <path class="t" d="M146 8 l8 -3 M146 14 l8 -3 M146 20 l8 -3"/>
        <text class="lab" x="160" y="16">twist builds up</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Before the spindle slows down, <b>catch it between your knees</b> so it can't unwind. The twist waits in the leader.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">7</span> Draft</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 140" role="img" aria-label="Front hand pinching above the twist, back hand pulling fibre upward to make a thin drafting triangle">
        <line class="t" x1="150" y1="138" x2="150" y2="96"/>
        <path class="t" d="M146 132 l8 -3 M146 122 l8 -3 M146 112 l8 -3 M146 102 l8 -3"/>
        <path class="f" d="M134 86 q-12 4 -12 14 q2 10 14 10 q12 -2 14 -12 q-2 -12 -16 -12 z"/>
        <text class="lab" x="164" y="104">front hand pinches</text>
        <path class="wool" d="M150 84 L134 40 L166 40 Z"/>
        <path class="wool" d="M134 40 C130 24, 132 10, 140 4 L160 4 C168 10, 170 24, 166 40 Z"/>
        <path class="f" d="M140 16 q-14 0 -16 12 q2 12 16 14 q14 0 16 -12 q-2 -14 -16 -14 z"/>
        <path class="arrow" d="M196 46 L196 12"/>
        <text class="lab" x="204" y="32">back hand</text>
        <text class="lab" x="204" y="44">draws back</text>
        <text class="lab" x="34" y="66">drafting</text>
        <text class="lab" x="34" y="78">triangle</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Pinch just above the twist with your <b>front hand</b>. With your <b>back hand</b>, slowly pull the fibre away, so a thin fan of fibre slides out between your hands. Draw out a few inches.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">8</span> Release the twist</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 140" role="img" aria-label="Front hand slides up and the twist runs up into the thin drafted fibre, making yarn">
        <line class="t" x1="150" y1="138" x2="150" y2="24"/>
        <path class="t" d="M146 132 l8 -3 M146 120 l8 -3 M146 108 l8 -3 M146 96 l8 -3 M146 84 l8 -3 M146 72 l8 -3 M146 60 l8 -3 M146 48 l8 -3 M146 36 l8 -3"/>
        <path class="arrow" d="M184 112 L184 40"/>
        <text class="lab" x="192" y="80">twist runs up</text>
        <path class="f" d="M142 8 q-14 0 -16 12 q2 12 16 14 q14 0 16 -12 q-2 -14 -16 -14 z"/>
        <text class="lab" x="40" y="80">new yarn</text>
      </svg>
      <p>Slide your front hand up and let the twist run into the drafted fibre. <b>That's yarn!</b> Keep the twist out of the fibre supply in your back hand. Then spin, park, draft and release again.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <h2><span class="num">9</span> Wind on</h2>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 300 140" role="img" aria-label="Yarn wound in a cone on the shaft below the whorl">
        <line class="l" x1="150" y1="10" x2="150" y2="134"/>
        <path class="l" d="M150 10 q0 -6 6 -6 q5 0 5 5"/>
        <ellipse class="f" cx="150" cy="20" rx="30" ry="6"/>
        <path class="f" d="M150 30 L176 40 L176 66 L150 96 L124 66 L124 40 Z"/>
        <path class="t" d="M126 46 L174 50 M126 54 L174 58 M128 62 L172 66 M134 72 L166 74 M140 82 L160 84"/>
        <text class="lab" x="186" y="58">wind into a cone</text>
        <path class="t" d="M150 30 C170 26, 178 18, 164 12 L158 8"/>
      </svg>
      <p>When the spindle nears the floor, unhook the yarn and <b>wind it onto the shaft</b> (under a top whorl, or above a bottom whorl). Keep about 18 in free, re-hook it, and carry on.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="two">
    <div class="box">
      <h3>Adding more fibre</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">When a strip runs out, fluff its last few inches and lay the next strip over them, just like the join in step 4. Let the twist run in. A slightly lumpy join is fine.</p>
      <h3 style="margin-top:9px">Finishing</h3>
      <p style="margin:0">Wind the yarn off into a loop (a <b>skein</b>). Soak it in warm water for 15 minutes, squeeze it gently in a towel, and hang it to dry with a light weight on it. This <b>sets the twist</b>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="box">
      <h3>If something goes wrong</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Yarn drifts apart:</b> it needs more twist, or it's too thin. Spin longer before you park.</li>
        <li><b>Yarn kinks on itself:</b> too much twist. Draft a little more fibre each time.</li>
        <li><b>Spindle unwinds:</b> you parked too late. Catch it while it's still turning.</li>
        <li><b>Lumps and thin spots:</b> totally normal. Beginner yarn is "art yarn."</li>
        <li><b>Spindle drops:</b> that's why it's called a drop spindle. Pick it up and re-join.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="box" style="margin-top:12px">
    <h3>Spinning alpaca</h3>
    <p style="margin:0">Alpaca is soft and warm, but it's <b>slippery</b>. It has little crimp and no lanolin, so the fibres slide apart more easily than wool. Give it <b>more twist</b> than you think it needs. Draft in <b>short pulls</b>, keeping your hands close together, and spin finer rather than thicker. If it's frustrating at first, practise a few lengths with sheep's wool (Corriedale is a good one), then come back to the alpaca.</p>
  </div>

  <footer><span>waterbearfieldschool.org/guides/drop-spindle</span><span>2 / 2</span></footer>
</section>
</body>
</html>
